.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-decapsulate 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-decapsulate \- Decapsulate an ML\-KEM\-768 ciphertext with a slot\*(Aqs key
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-decapsulate\fR [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISLOT\fR> <\fICIPHERTEXT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decapsulate an ML\-KEM\-768 ciphertext with a slot\*(Aqs key
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-pin\fR \fI<PIN>\fR
PIN code (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISLOT\fR>
PIV slot holding an ML\-KEM\-768 key
.TP
<\fICIPHERTEXT\fR>
File containing the 1088\-byte ciphertext (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin)
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>
File to write the 32\-byte shared secret to (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdout)
